; REPCOUNT: the innermost currently-running REPEAT's 1-indexed pass
; number, -1 outside any REPEAT. Follow-up to the 2026-08-11 Terrapin
; comparison's easy tier -- flagged there as needing real VM support
; (a per-Vm counter stack), unlike that batch's own plain wrappers.

REPEAT 5 [PRINT REPCOUNT]
PRINT REPCOUNT

; A spiral, sized by its own pass number -- the classic REPCOUNT idiom.
REPEAT 36 [FD REPCOUNT * 3 RT 10]

; Dynamic, not lexical: a procedure called from inside a REPEAT sees
; the CALLER's REPCOUNT.
TO ANNOUNCE
  PRINT SENTENCE "pass: REPCOUNT
END
REPEAT 3 [announce]
